      "The tradeoff: Razer Synapse software is heavier than Logi Options+, and the Pro Click's ergonomic angle is slightly less aggressive. For Mac users, check our Mac-specific guide (https://verticalmouseguide.com/guides/best-vertical-mouse-for-mac) for software compatibility details.",
      "Kensington Pro Fit Ergo \u2014 Best Mid-Range Wireless",
      "The Pro Fit Ergo sits at roughly half the price of the MX Vertical and Razer Pro Click while offering dual-mode wireless connectivity. AA battery power means no charging cable needed \u2014 swap batteries every 6 months. The 1600 DPI sensor is adequate for single-monitor setups but struggles on dual 4K displays.",
      "A strong choice for users who want wireless convenience without the premium price, particularly in office environments where multi-device pairing and Bluetooth simplicity matter.",
      "Anker Ergonomic Vertical \u2014 Best Budget Wireless",
      "At under $25, the Anker is the lowest-risk wireless entry point. The 2.4 GHz-only connection (no Bluetooth) means you need the USB-A dongle, but latency is excellent at 2\u20134 ms. Battery life on a single AA lasts 3+ months. The body is smaller than premium options \u2014 hands over 20 cm will overhang \u2014 but the ergonomic benefit of the vertical angle is fully present.",
      "Evoluent VerticalMouse 4 (Wired) \u2014 Best Wired Option",
