      "For desk workers using a mouse 4+ hours daily, yes. The 1\u20132 week adjustment is temporary. The reduced forearm strain, less end-of-day fatigue, and RSI prevention are permanent. Users who switched for existing wrist pain frequently report meaningful symptom reduction.",
      "What if I still cannot adjust after 2 weeks?",
      "Check three things: mouse size (too large or small forces an uncomfortable grip), DPI setting (try 800 if control is still imprecise), and desk height (elbow should be at 90 degrees). If all are correct and discomfort persists, the vertical form factor may not suit your hand anatomy \u2014 consider a trackball alternative.",
