      "The thumb buttons (forward/back navigation) on most vertical mice sit 25\u201335 mm forward of the thumb's natural resting position \u2014 designed for a longer thumb. A shorter thumb must extend fully to reach them, creating sustained extensor strain in the very muscle group that the vertical grip is supposed to relax.",
