      "If you have constant numbness, grip weakness (dropping objects), thenar muscle wasting (the muscle pad at the thumb base is visibly smaller), or symptoms that wake you every night \u2014 a vertical mouse is not the answer. These symptoms indicate significant median nerve compression that requires medical evaluation and likely intervention (corticosteroid injection, physical therapy, or surgical release).",
